  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 81b9501dec89da64eb81f4c230bdd187, type: 3}
  m_Name: Memory Draught
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::HoneyAndHemlock.Customers.CustomerSO
  _requestedPotion: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 6308f8108fc2d5140ab55dc4cc259a58, type: 2}
  _request:
  - My mother used to make a recipe. A special stew for the deep of winter. She passed
    last season and I can't recall it. Not even a single ingredient. It's like someone
    scooped it right out of my head.
  - I witnessed a dreadful caravan attack on the road three weeks back. I need to
    remember every detail so the garrison can hunt the bandits down. But every time
    I try to think back, it all goes foggy.
  _playerResponse:
  - I can bring it back
  - I can help you remember
  _successfulResponse:
  - I remember. All of it. The way she'd toast the barley first, the pinch of winterbloom,
    the way the kitchen smelled. It's like she's standing right next to me again.
    Thank you.
  - Every face. Every detail. The color of their cloaks, the banner they carried,
    the direction they fled. I have everything the garrison needs. You've helped
    me get justice.
  _failedResponse:
  - It's not coming back. Though, now I'm remembering things that aren't mine. A
    childhood that isn't my own. A face I've never seen before. Whose memories are
    these?
  - I remember more now, but it's all wrong. The details have changed. The faces
    are different. I don't know which memories are real anymore and which ones you
    put there.
  _cosmicResponse:
  - "Something ancient saw me. It remembered me. It seems like over lifetimes\u2026
    but I still can\u2019t remember the recipe. Can you still help me?"
  - "I saw everything for such a short time. I don\u2019t think I can ever forget
    that\u2026 but I don\u2019t want to forget about those bandits. I still need
    to remember their faces."
